.TH CLOCWORK 1 "2026-09-15" "clocwork 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
clocwork \- lines per language, AI co\-authored commits and token cost over a repository's history
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clocwork
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIREPO\fR]
.br
.B clocwork tokens
[\-o DIR] [\-\-config PATH] [\-\-locale TAG] [\-\-no\-open] [\-q] [REPO]
.br
.B clocwork render
[\-o DIR] [\-\-config PATH] [\-\-locale TAG] [\-\-no\-open] [\-q]
.br
.B clocwork \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lines per language, AI co\-authored commits and token cost over a repository's history.
.PP
Every commit reachable from the analysed ref is measured with
.BR cloc (1)
in git diff mode and cached per file, so a first run over a long history is slow and every later run takes seconds. The result is a self\-contained
.I index.html
written to a workspace next to the repository, never inside it: lines per language and type at every commit, which commits an AI agent co\-authored and when each model first appeared, and, when Claude Code transcripts exist for the repository, what the work cost in tokens.
.PP
A first argument that is not a command is taken as
.IR REPO ,
so
.B clocwork ~/code/foo
works; the default is the current directory, and any directory inside the repository will do.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS run
.B clocwork run
[\-o DIR] [\-\-config PATH] [\-\-locale TAG] [\-\-no\-open] [\-q] [\-\-branch REF] [\-\-max\-commits N] [\-\-no\-tokens] [\-\-cache\-dir DIR] [REPO]
.PP
analyse, archive tokens and render (the default)
.TP
.I REPO
repository or any directory inside it (default: cwd)
.TP
.B \-o, \-\-output DIR
workspace directory (default: <repo\-parent>/<repo\-name>\-stats)
.TP
.B \-\-config PATH
explicit clocwork.toml
.TP
.B \-\-locale TAG
region locale for the page (default: $CLOCWORK_LOCALE, else the machine's region)
.TP
.B \-\-no\-open
do not open the dashboard in a browser
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet
print nothing but errors
.TP
.B \-\-branch REF
ref to analyse (default: the checked\-out branch)
.TP
.B \-\-max\-commits N
measure at most N uncached commits this run
.TP
.B \-\-no\-tokens
skip the transcript scan
.TP
.B \-\-cache\-dir DIR
cache location (default: $XDG_CACHE_HOME/clocwork, else ~/.cache/clocwork)
.SS tokens
.B clocwork tokens
[\-o DIR] [\-\-config PATH] [\-\-locale TAG] [\-\-no\-open] [\-q] [REPO]
.PP
archive Claude Code transcripts only
.TP
.I REPO
repository or any directory inside it (default: cwd)
.TP
.B \-o, \-\-output DIR
workspace directory (default: <repo\-parent>/<repo\-name>\-stats)
.TP
.B \-\-config PATH
explicit clocwork.toml
.TP
.B \-\-locale TAG
region locale for the page (default: $CLOCWORK_LOCALE, else the machine's region)
.TP
.B \-\-no\-open
do not open the dashboard in a browser
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet
print nothing but errors
.SS render
.B clocwork render
[\-o DIR] [\-\-config PATH] [\-\-locale TAG] [\-\-no\-open] [\-q]
.PP
re\-render the dashboard from existing workspace data
.TP
.B \-o, \-\-output DIR
workspace directory (default: <repo\-parent>/<repo\-name>\-stats)
.TP
.B \-\-config PATH
explicit clocwork.toml
.TP
.B \-\-locale TAG
region locale for the page (default: $CLOCWORK_LOCALE, else the machine's region)
.TP
.B \-\-no\-open
do not open the dashboard in a browser
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet
print nothing but errors
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CLOCWORK_LOCALE
A BCP 47 tag such as
.BR en\-SE .
The region locale the page formats numbers, dates and units with. Wins over the machine's setting;
.B \-\-locale
wins over both.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
When set, the cloc cache lives under
.IR $XDG_CACHE_HOME/clocwork/ ;
otherwise under
.IR ~/.cache/clocwork/ .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I <repo\-parent>/<repo\-name>\-stats/
The workspace: a sibling of the repository, overridden with
.BR \-o .
.TP
.I clocwork.json
Which repository the workspace belongs to. A run against another repository is refused rather than overwriting the workspace.
.TP
.I clocwork.toml
Optional configuration: page title, test\-path rules, extra agents. The first found wins:
.BR \-\-config ,
then this file in the workspace, then
.I .clocwork.toml
in the repository.
.TP
.I token_usage.json
The per\-day token archive scanned from Claude Code transcripts. It cannot be regenerated once the transcripts expire; no run shrinks it.
.TP
.I full_commit_data.json
The analysis the page is rendered from.
.TP
.IR index.html ", " commit_bodies.js
The dashboard and its sidecar of full commit messages.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/clocwork/<name>\-<hash>/cloc_cache.json
Per\-file cloc results keyed by commit, so a changed test rule or language table re\-reads the cache instead of re\-running cloc.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 2
An error the command reported: cloc missing, no git repository, a repository with no commits, a workspace belonging to another repository, invalid configuration, or an unreadable or unwritable file. A usage error also exits 2, with the usage line on standard error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cloc (1),
.BR git (1),
.BR git\-log (1)
